**ClawdBot Redefines AI Assistant Expectations**
@dstartupkid reports ClawdBot is trending as a Claude-powered browser automation agent that "makes people rethink what assistants and AI interfaces should feel like." The tool represents a shift from conversational AI to autonomous web task execution.

**Kanye West Previews AI-Generated Music Video**
@rowancheung notes Kanye West posted an AI-generated video preview on Instagram, stating "AI has been trending hot in Hollywood lately. The next few months are going to be wild for AI video." Celebrity adoption signals mainstream creative industry integration.

**Google Photos 'Me Meme' AI Feature Launches**
@DigitalTrends announces Google Photos is rolling out "Me Meme," an AI feature enabling users to recreate trending memes using their own photos. The tool democratizes meme creation through personalized AI generation.

**South Korea's Open-Source AI Strategy Gains Traction**
@ClementDelangue (HuggingFace CEO) highlights South Korea has three trending models on the platform due to state support for open-source AI, noting "all countries can (and should) be builders thanks to open-source" beyond US-China competition.

**WPP Chief AI Officer on Agentic AI Readiness**
@WPP's Chief AI Officer Daniel Hulme discusses business preparedness for agentic AI, warning companies to "avoid common pitfalls and be strategic" about the transformative technology as adoption accelerates.
